// endpoint_select_feed_row.proto — SelectFeedRow: move, clear or end the
// selection of one workspace's feed. FEED section.
//
// The DAEMON owns the selection per workspace (frontend.v1.FeedSelection): it
// knows the ordered rows, so it COMPUTES which row a step lands on rather than
// a client naming one, and it is the only holder of the selection, so what
// the webapp draws and what a sent prompt or a rollback acts on can never
// disagree. The result is pushed to the webapp on the feed watch and to
// Emacs on the host workspace watch, and acked here.
//
// Emacs steps the selection (`C-p` / `C-n` through final responses, `C-S-p` /
// `C-S-n` through prompts) and clears it (escape twice); the webapp clears it
// (a click on the feed's background) and ends it when the selected row has
// left the viewport entirely.

